description:
Write four functions:

```lua-norun
parse_age(s)             -- the whole number in the text s, from 0 to 150. Otherwise it raises an error with NO position
                         -- added (level 0), whose message is "not a number: <s>", "not a whole number: <s>"
                         -- or "out of range: <n>"
read_ages(list)          -- parses every string in list with parse_age and returns two lists:
                         -- the ages that worked, and the error messages of those that did not, both in order
validate(user)           -- returns true for a table with a non-empty string name and an age from parse_age;
                         -- otherwise raises an error that is a TABLE: { field = "name" or "age", problem = <text> }
with_retry(f, attempts)  -- calls f() until it succeeds, at most attempts times, and returns its first result;
                         -- if every attempt fails, raises the last error again unchanged
```

```lua-norun
read_ages({ "42", "abc", "200" })   --> { 42 }, { "not a number: abc", "out of range: 200" }
pcall(validate, { age = "7" })      --> false, { field = "name", problem = "missing" }
```

